#
#  DWD ICON global (R03B07, about 13 km) PRESSURE-LEVEL GRIB2 for the Rust
#  met_intermediate writer, map source "dwd".  Source: Deutscher Wetterdienst
#  (DWD), CC BY 4.0.  The model-level twin is Vtable.ICON-GLOBAL-ML.rw.
#
#  ICON's native GDT 3.101 mesh is not a lat-lon grid: these rows read the
#  regional regular lat-lon GRIB2 that gdt101_remap writes, which keeps each
#  object's product section, so the identifiers below are DWD's own.  GRIB2
#  only: the GRIB1 parameter column is blank on every row.
#
#  * Eighteen pressure levels, 1000-30 hPa: T, RELHUM, U, V and FI.  GHT is
#    derived from FI (geopotential, m2 s-2) as FI / 9.81 (rule ght_from_fi).
#    ICON reports RELHUM over liquid water, so no over-ice conversion runs.
#  * 2 m RH is RELHUM_2M as published; 2 m dewpoint (TD_2M) is read so the
#    rrpr.F dewpoint derivation can stand in when RELHUM_2M is absent.
#  * PSFC is PS, SKINTEMP is T_G (the sea surface temperature over water),
#    SOILHGT is HSURF, SNOW is W_SNOW (kg m-2, which is mm of water), SNOWH
#    is H_SNOW (m) and SEAICE is FR_ICE.  LANDSEA is FR_LAND; the "dwd" map
#    source converts it to a flag (> 0.5 is land).  HSURF and FR_LAND are
#    time-invariant and ride the step-0 objects (--invariant).
#  * Soil.  T_SO is published at nine single depths (fixed surface 106, no
#    second surface): 0, 0.5, 2, 6, 18, 54, 162, 486 and 1458 cm.  A
#    single-depth row names its depth in Level1, in cm, one decimal allowed,
#    and matches that depth only.  W_SO is published per TERRA layer as
#    kg m-2 between two depths; its rows carry both bounds in cm.
#    Rows T_SO_N* and W_SO_L* have blank descriptions: they are read and
#    consumed, never published.
#  * The SOILT/SOILM rows are DERIVED rows (blank GRIB2 parameter): their
#    Level1/Level2 columns declare the target layer in cm, and the "dwd"
#    rules fill them.  SOILM = W_SO / (1000 kg m-3 * thickness m) from the
#    W_SO layer with the same bounds (rule soilm_from_w_so).  SOILT is T_SO
#    at the layer midpoint, linear in depth between bracketing nodes (rule
#    soilt_from_t_so); TERRA's nodes below the surface ARE the layer
#    midpoints, so each layer copies one node and the 0 cm node feeds none.
#    The names and thicknesses (1, 2, 6, 18, 54, 162, 486, 1458 cm) are the
#    ones rw_mpas_init dispatches; 999 stands for the 1458 cm layer.
#  * Only instantaneous messages (product templates 4.0/4.1) match.
